Data Engineering Roadmap

Phase 1 — Foundations

Python for Data Engineering
Files: CSV, JSON, Parquet
Functions, OOP basics
pandas
Error handling & logging
Virtual environments
SQL
JOINs
CTEs
Window functions
Aggregations
Query optimization
Linux
Bash
Processes
Permissions
grep, awk, sed, curl
Cron jobs
Git/GitHub

Phase 2 — Databases

PostgreSQL
MySQL
Database design
Normalization
Indexes
Transactions
Views
Query plans

Phase 3 — ETL / ELT
You'll learn to build pipelines like:

API / CSV / Database
        ↓
     Extract
        ↓
   Python Pipeline
        ↓
   Transform/Clean
        ↓
      Storage
        ↓
   PostgreSQL / Data Warehouse

Important concepts:

ETL vs ELT
Batch processing
Incremental loading
Data validation
Data quality
Idempotency

Phase 4 — Big Data

Apache Spark
PySpark
Partitioning
Shuffling
Distributed processing
Spark SQL
Performance optimization

Phase 5 — Data Warehousing

OLTP vs OLAP
Star schema
Fact & dimension tables
Slowly Changing Dimensions
Data marts
BigQuery / Snowflake / Redshift concepts

Phase 6 — Orchestration

Apache Airflow
DAGs
Tasks
Scheduling
Retries
Dependencies
Monitoring

Example:

Every day 2 AM

API
 ↓
Extract
 ↓
Validate
 ↓
Transform
 ↓
Load PostgreSQL
 ↓
Run Spark job
 ↓
Update warehouse
 ↓
Send success/failure alert

Phase 7 — Cloud + Modern DE
Pick one cloud first, rather than trying everything.

I'd recommend:

AWS
 ├── S3
 ├── IAM
 ├── Glue
 ├── Athena
 ├── RDS
 └── Redshift

Then learn:

Docker
Kubernetes basics
Kafka
CI/CD
Terraform basics